WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:04.089
Speaker 1: Christian nationalism is something
we've spoken about a lot on the program.

00:00:04.089 --> 00:00:10.719
Christian nationalism is very, generally speaking,
a view where you believe that Christianity

00:00:10.719 --> 00:00:14.670
should be not only one of many religions that
people in their private lives can choose to

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:20.150
follow, but directly connected to the law
of the land and civil government.

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:24.760
Christian nationalism includes the idea that
the doctrine of Christianity should be first

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:30.140
and foremost and in the forefront of what
determines what are civil laws and civil government.

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:35.950
Now, Congresswoman Lauren Boebert from Colorado,
who recently just barely, barely, barely won

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:36.970
reelection.

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:39.810
She recently made some comments about Jesus
and Christianity.

00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:41.559
And it's really the stuff of nightmares.

00:00:41.559 --> 00:00:44.630
She spoke about the end times and the rapture.

00:00:44.630 --> 00:00:46.950
And let's look at the clip first.

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:50.870
But I want you to just have in mind and I
know I've said this before and people get

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:52.289
offended.

00:00:52.289 --> 00:00:57.840
What is the line between religion and delusional
mental illness when it comes to the sorts

00:00:57.840 --> 00:00:59.000
of stuff she talks about?

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.570
I don't pretend to know the answer, but let's
listen to what she said.

00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:06.680
Speaker 2: And one thing that I love, just
an analogy.

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:08.310
Maybe, maybe it's true.

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:11.470
Maybe it's not about the second coming of
Jesus.

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:17.070
I've heard stories of people believing that
Christians are going to be hiding out in caves

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:19.220
and, you know, in just lockdown.

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:21.320
Maybe maybe it's a lockdown, maybe it's a
government lockdown.

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:24.530
But they're shut in and they beg for Jesus
to come back.

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:26.130
He comes back and rescues them.

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:28.380
I don't think that that's the way it's going
to be.

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:32.420
As if the Old Testament is a type in the shadow
of the New Testament.

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:36.140
And you look at the exodus from Egypt.

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:41.490
Pharaoh, he was the one who called for God
to get his people.

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:45.119
He said, Get your people out of here.

00:01:45.119 --> 00:01:49.939
And I believe if if that type in shadow is
true for the New Testament, the Church, God's

00:01:49.939 --> 00:01:55.590
people will be out in such a great force that
Satan himself will call for the second coming

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:56.590
of Jesus.

00:01:56.590 --> 00:01:59.530
You say, I cannot do a thing in this earth
with your people.

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:01.070
Here you come and get them.

00:02:01.070 --> 00:02:02.100
Speaker 1: Come on.

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:03.100
Wow.

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:04.100
Incredibly powerful stuff.

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:06.840
Now, I really need you to understand what
she's talking about here.

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:13.300
This second coming of Jesus stuff, resurrection,
rapture, end times.

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:15.200
This is all you know, there's different flavors.

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:18.930
And I know no matter which summary I give,
someone will write in and say, David, you're

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:21.260
misunderstanding this or that aspect of it.

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:26.629
Remember, there's a thousand versions of this,
but it is some combination of there is going

00:02:26.629 --> 00:02:34.830
to be some kind of end time event where the
Christians that are alive and the resurrected

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:39.020
believers are going to rise in the clouds.

00:02:39.020 --> 00:02:44.360
And here on earth, bad things are going to
happen in some of these versions.

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:52.800
All of the Jews die and some of these Virgin
Virgins versions, 144,000 Jews survive.

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:55.569
There's every everything under the sun.

00:02:55.569 --> 00:02:57.290
It's all pretty bonkers.

00:02:57.290 --> 00:02:58.310
Okay.

00:02:58.310 --> 00:03:05.400
From just an earthly perspective, and it is
apparently in some circles not only acceptable

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:09.620
but welcomed to hear elected officials talking
in this way.

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:15.660
And they use these beliefs to inform what
they believe the law should be.

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:21.410
For example, the very same place that Lauren
Boebert gets, the ideas you just heard, she

00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:25.750
gets her ideas about abortion, which then
she uses to say, Here's what the law should

00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:28.549
be, even though we're supposed to have separation
of church and state.

00:03:28.549 --> 00:03:31.129
So comments like these are just completely
appalling.

00:03:31.129 --> 00:03:35.739
And her desire to inject this sort of stuff
into civil government is an obvious violation

00:03:35.739 --> 00:03:37.890
of the separation of church and state.

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:43.750
It if if, if she got her way, it would lead
to unofficial discrimination and marginalization

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:48.129
of non-Christians, of non religious people
altogether.

00:03:48.129 --> 00:03:52.569
And it is one of the scariest things that
is going on right now as a movement within

00:03:52.569 --> 00:03:53.569
the Republican Party.

00:03:53.569 --> 00:03:54.920
Yeah, MAGA stuff, it's wacky.

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:55.920
It's scary.

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:56.920
Space lasers, all of it, right?

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:57.920
It's crazy.

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:00.829
But the Christian nationalism stuff is particularly
dangerous.

00:04:00.829 --> 00:04:02.650
Here is another clip from the same interview.

00:04:02.650 --> 00:04:06.000
This was the Faith in Action podcast, I guess.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:12.420
Lauren Boebert says God tells her reelection
would be like the Prophet Elijah in the Bible,

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:14.050
defeating the prophets of Baal.

00:04:14.050 --> 00:04:15.860
This is this is what God said to her.

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:19.060
I don't know if this was like at a cafe, at
a bar or in private prayer.

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:20.060
Speaker 2: Well, totally.

00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:22.930
But and then this one, it was just the Democrat
and myself.

00:04:22.930 --> 00:04:25.070
He campaigned as a Republican.

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:26.590
The media allowed him to do that.

00:04:26.590 --> 00:04:27.850
They called him a conservative.

00:04:27.850 --> 00:04:28.850
Right.

00:04:28.850 --> 00:04:31.270
Just allowed him to define himself as that
is bizarre.

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:37.080
But I guess, again, with 51% of the vote,
barely just took a lot longer to get there.

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:41.110
But, you know, throughout all of this, I was
telling you, you know, God was really pressing

00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:42.110
on my heart.

00:04:42.110 --> 00:04:43.110
The story of Elijah.

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:44.160
Speaker 1: Okay.

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:45.780
She's saying God spoke to her.

00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:46.780
Okay.

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:48.040
I really need get everybody to understand.

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:55.889
She is saying that a man in the sky, I think
they still say he's a man of sorts or a masculine

00:04:55.889 --> 00:04:59.040
entity in the sky.

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:04.250
Spoke to her about specific passages in the
context of her reelection.

00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:10.300
Speaker 2: He said the true God will answer
by fire and those who worshiped Bale.

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:11.800
They they believe that Bale was.

00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:14.020
Speaker 1: Oh, I said Ball, I guess it's Bale,
the.

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:15.280
Speaker 2: True God, he said.

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:16.400
I said, Prove it.

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:19.790
If Bale is a true God, tell him to answer
by fire.

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:21.620
And they're calling for him.

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:22.620
They're screaming, They're hollering.

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:24.759
They're cutting themselves or act in a pool.

00:05:24.759 --> 00:05:28.210
You know, we've seen that like in 2020 riots.

00:05:28.210 --> 00:05:29.370
Stop, Right?

00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:31.759
But their God didn't show up.

00:05:31.759 --> 00:05:33.630
Elijah was mocking them yet.

00:05:33.630 --> 00:05:35.190
Well, maybe cry a little bit louder.

00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:36.190
Maybe he can't hear you.

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:37.190
Maybe he's sleeping.

00:05:37.190 --> 00:05:38.190
Maybe he's on vacation.

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:39.190
I love that so much.

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:40.290
And then he went.

00:05:40.290 --> 00:05:41.880
He said, You know what?

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:43.190
I'm going to do you one better.

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:47.440
I don't want you to say that this is some
kind of fluke, some sort of combustion that

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:48.440
just happened.

00:05:48.440 --> 00:05:51.780
I'm going to drench the altar with fire or
with water three times.

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:53.610
Speaker 1: Fire or water, whichever three.

00:05:53.610 --> 00:05:57.539
Speaker 2: Times to wet and drench the altar
with fire and God with water.

00:05:57.539 --> 00:05:58.940
And God still showed up by fire.

00:05:58.940 --> 00:06:01.100
And that's what he was showing you at this
election.

00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:05.520
He said it may look impossible in the natural
that there will not be a victory.

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:09.100
You may hear the voices, you may hear other
people, but I am going to show up.

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:15.070
Speaker 1: Now, of course, these are always
stories that are that are told with the hindsight

00:06:15.070 --> 00:06:17.380
of knowing how the election turned up.

00:06:17.380 --> 00:06:20.220
She barely won and she could have lost.

00:06:20.220 --> 00:06:21.900
Would she still be telling the story?

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:26.940
Listen, God came to me and he said, Your reelection
is going to be like when Prophet Elijah defeated

00:06:26.940 --> 00:06:28.750
the prophets of Bel, then she loses.

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:30.139
Oh, I guess God was wrong.

00:06:30.139 --> 00:06:33.580
No, but God, God is never wrong and blah,
blah, blah, blah, blah.

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:39.000
This is the sort of stuff, even if they don't
say it, that a lot of members of Congress

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:42.030
are thinking when they think about how they
are legislating.

00:06:42.030 --> 00:06:46.110
Now, I know many of you will write in and
say, but you know, David, this it's really

00:06:46.110 --> 00:06:50.210
not a big deal because you look at in Italy,
everybody's Catholic.

00:06:50.210 --> 00:06:53.770
You know, all the elected officials are Catholic
and it is no big deal.

00:06:53.770 --> 00:06:57.840
It's really important to understand that not
all religions are the same.

00:06:57.840 --> 00:06:59.669
And I know lots of Italian Catholics.

00:06:59.669 --> 00:07:02.150
I have many Italian Catholic friends.

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:08.000
What it means to them to be Catholic is a
very different thing than what it means for

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:09.500
evangelicals.

00:07:09.500 --> 00:07:15.240
Like I believe she's evangelical Lauren Boebert
to be evangelical and the comfort that folks

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:19.440
like Boebert have, even despite the separation
of church and state that we're supposed to

00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:24.410
have, saying things like we need Christian
nationalism, we need the church to be guiding

00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:25.410
government.

00:07:25.410 --> 00:07:30.460
And all of the things I've covered her saying
over recent years, a lot of people with some

00:07:30.460 --> 00:07:33.600
connection to reality would be embarrassed
to be on video saying the things that Lauren

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:38.690
Boebert says, not not for the religious reasons,
but because it would be seen as so inappropriate

00:07:38.690 --> 00:07:45.180
to come out and say, I believe that my religion,
not just religion, but my religion, not anybody

00:07:45.180 --> 00:07:49.590
else's, not any other religions, should be
dictating how government works.

00:07:49.590 --> 00:07:53.949
You talk to Catholic politicians in Italy
who are nominally Catholic and would consider

00:07:53.949 --> 00:07:56.790
themselves religious in the way that many
Europeans do.

00:07:56.790 --> 00:08:00.260
They would be humiliated to be caught saying
things like what Lauren Boebert says.

00:08:00.260 --> 00:08:01.330
So it's not all the same.

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:06.000
And it's a really important thing to understand
this particular brand of Christian nationalism

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:10.400
that often comes from born again Christians
and evangelicals, etc.

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:16.460
It's not just kind of wacky in terms of the
things they say it is, but it's not only that.

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:23.870
It also is extraordinarily dangerous in terms
of what it would mean if they got their way.

00:08:23.870 --> 00:08:28.310
And when you look at what's happening in the
Supreme Court and Amy Coney Barrett and others

00:08:28.310 --> 00:08:34.330
who are on that court, who at least to some
degree share a lot of these views, you realize

00:08:34.330 --> 00:08:39.099
that if things keep going the direction that
they've been going, it's not completely out

00:08:39.099 --> 00:08:43.890
of the question that in some ways the boebert
types could get their way.

00:08:43.890 --> 00:08:45.201
And that's a horrifying thing to think about.

